WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
Joining.

2
00:00:00.996 --> 00:00:03.411
A model is lots of pieces joined together.

3
00:00:03.571 --> 00:00:05.196
Glue sticks flat things.

4
00:00:05.356 --> 00:00:06.935
Tape is quick and strong.

5
00:00:07.095 --> 00:00:08.628
String ties and hangs.

6
00:00:08.788 --> 00:00:10.877
Wet clay presses onto wet clay.

7
00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:12.616
Card slots into card.

8
00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:13.891
Paper folds.

9
00:00:14.051 --> 00:00:16.884
Six joins, and each one is best at something.

10
00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.559
The tools.

11
00:00:18.719 --> 00:00:22.527
A glue stick, sticky tape, string, a split pin, clay and scissors.

12
00:00:22.687 --> 00:00:24.870
The scissors do not join, they cut.

13
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.373
You sit down to use them, and you never walk while holding them.

14
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:30.763
That is the first rule of the art room.

15
00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:32.856
Why won't it join?.

16
00:00:33.016 --> 00:00:34.966
Sometimes a join does not hold.

17
00:00:35.126 --> 00:00:36.473
The wheels fall off.

18
00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:37.840
The pot cracks.

19
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.044
An artist does not throw it away.

20
00:00:40.204 --> 00:00:42.851
They look, think about why, and change one thing.

21
00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:45.194
If that did not fix it, they change another.

22
00:00:45.354 --> 00:00:47.397
Every try teaches you something.

23
00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:49.258
A pinch pot.

24
00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:50.811
Roll a ball of clay.

25
00:00:50.971 --> 00:00:52.782
Push your thumb into the middle.

26
00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:55.496
Pinch the sides up, turning it round and round.

27
00:00:55.656 --> 00:00:57.143
Smooth it with wet fingers.

28
00:00:57.303 --> 00:00:58.324
Let it dry.

29
00:00:58.484 --> 00:01:00.435
That is the first pot every potter makes.
